WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.728 --> 00:00:04.195
- [Narrator] Okinoshima
Island is a short 12 minute

00:00:04.195 --> 00:00:06.288
ferry ride from Hiroshima region of Japan.

00:00:06.288 --> 00:00:08.912
While the sandy and
palm-lined beaches are perfect

00:00:08.912 --> 00:00:11.070
for holiday makers,
the island draws crowds

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:13.737
for a different reason: rabbits.

00:00:14.852 --> 00:00:15.852
Lots of 'em.

00:00:17.073 --> 00:00:20.393
And how they got there is a mystery.

00:00:20.393 --> 00:00:23.427
(upbeat music)

00:00:23.427 --> 00:00:25.625
(playful music)

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:28.375
Between 1929 and 1945, Japanese armies

00:00:28.375 --> 00:00:31.358
secretly produced over
6,000 tons of poison gas

00:00:31.358 --> 00:00:33.439
on Okinoshima Island.

00:00:33.439 --> 00:00:35.570
Some believe the current
rabbits are descendants

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.576
of those brought to the
island to test the gas.

00:00:37.576 --> 00:00:39.314
But the current director
of the Poison Gas Museum

00:00:39.314 --> 00:00:41.799
insists these bunnies have
nothing to do with those

00:00:41.799 --> 00:00:43.384
from the World War II era.

00:00:43.384 --> 00:00:45.634
So where do they come from?

00:00:50.488 --> 00:00:52.488
- [Narrator] One theory.

00:01:08.751 --> 00:01:10.338
- [Narrator] So those
rabbits were released

00:01:10.338 --> 00:01:11.871
and with no real predators,

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:15.010
they bred like, well, like rabbits.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.927
And yet another theory.

00:01:34.595 --> 00:01:36.287
- [Narrator] Either
way, this new generation

00:01:36.287 --> 00:01:38.140
of feral rabbits has the run of the land.

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:39.866
They're creating a new story separate

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:41.908
from the sordid past of Okinoshima Island.

00:01:41.908 --> 00:01:44.187
An island once known
for death is now known

00:01:44.187 --> 00:01:47.854
for possibly the cutest
thing ever: bunnies.

00:01:49.111 --> 00:01:51.778
(playful music)

